{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The memory cards fit my repeated purchases of removable storage and adapters; they support devices I already use.",
    "The 64GB option offers a useful capacity increase over my earlier 16GB and 32GB cards, although its bundled reader duplicates something I already own."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Owning a Fire 7 does not mean I currently want another tablet; my case, mount, and storage purchases show interest in making my existing devices more useful.",
    "Streaming devices and a subwoofer do not address my current accessory needs, and 4K capability gives me little reason to upgrade alongside my 720p TV.",
    "Photography tripods and a lens cap do not imply that I need a security camera, doorbell, or connected lighting; those serve different purposes."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire tablet purchase seems to have been taken as broad interest in Amazon streaming and smart home devices.",
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been treated as interest in more electronics generally, without enough attention to what each item helps me do."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I repeatedly choose practical accessories such as cables, mounts, card holders, and power strips that support equipment I already have.",
    "Existing purchases matter when considering overlap: I already have a card reader and a tablet, so added capacity is more appealing than another device with the same purpose.",
    "Compatibility and intended use matter to me; a familiar brand or the word camera alone does not make an item useful for my photography and device needs."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The memory cards match my recurring storage needs, but most other suggestions mistake my practical accessory shopping for interest in replacing devices or adding smart home equipment."
}"}
